E</span><span class="brief__kind brief__kind--research">🔬 Research</span></p><h3 class="brief__code">KPMG</h3><p class="brief__title">AI Engineer Intern</p><p class="brief__sub">KPMG · Berlin, DE · Jun 2025 – Aug 2025</p></div><img class="org-logo" src="/logos/orgs/kpmg.png" alt="KPMG logo" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy"></header><h4 class="brief__label">Objective</h4><p>Re-recruited based on Summer 2024 performance; bypassed the formal interview cycle to lead an AI engineering project in Agile Scrum sprints for KPMG&#39;s Global Audit division serving international teams.</p><h4 class="brief__label">Results</h4><ul class="brief__results"><li>Architected a vector-graph RAG pipeline (LangGraph, Neo4j) with CoT prompting and Instructor-structured outputs, generating 500+ judge-validated QA pairs for an audit-expert LLM, saving 50+ hours.</li><li>Built a multi-threaded LLM-as-a-judge framework in the OpenAI SDK to validate every generated QA pair&#39;s answer quality before fine-tuning.</li><li>Built a GPT-4o vision parser with PyMuPDF rendering and exponential-backoff retries for 600+ audit manual pages, eliminating 10 hrs/week of manual correction.</li><li>Cut inference cost ~17x by routing bulk audit-question generation to GPT-4o-mini with step-decomposed prompts and Pydantic-validated outputs.</li><li>Modularized preprocessing into 5 documented notebooks sharing a structural chunking algorithm for both SFT and CPT pipelines.</li></ul><h4 class="brief__label">Payload</h4><ul class="stack-chips"><li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #3776AB"><svg class="stack-chip__logo" viewBox="-1 -1 14 14" shape-rendering="crispEdges" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="-1" y="-1" width="14" height="14" fill="#f4efe2"></rect><rect x="3" y="0" width="5" height="1" fill="#3776AB"></rect><rect x="3" y="1" width="1" height="1" fill="#3776AB"></rect><rect x="5" y="1" width="4" height="1" fill="#3776AB"></rect><rect x="3" y="2" width="6" height="1" fill="#3776AB"></rect><rect x="1" y="3