n><span class="brief__status brief__status--active">ACTIVE</span></p><h3 class="brief__code">J&amp;J</h3><p class="brief__title">AI Engineer</p><p class="brief__sub">Johnson &amp; Johnson · Raritan, NJ · Aug 2026 – Present</p></div><img class="org-logo" src="/logos/orgs/jnj.png" alt="Johnson &amp; Johnson logo" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy"></header><h4 class="brief__label">Objective</h4><p>Architected an end-to-end Databricks pipeline (Oracle to curated Delta tables to S3) powering an AI-driven complaint scoring system processing 30,000+ complaints annually, deployed via Jenkins CI/CD across dev/qa/prod.</p><h4 class="brief__label">Results</h4><ul class="brief__results"><li>Engineered an LLM-based scoring orchestration layer with batch processing, prompt caching, and checkpointing, cutting compute costs 50% and saving SMEs weeks of manual review annually.</li><li>Extended a shared Python-based AWS Bedrock AgentCore runtime with configurable model selection across the full request chain, giving a 55-member team flexibility to experiment with new AI tooling.</li><li>Built and deployed a Hugo static site in Go across 4 environments with Jenkins CI/CD and Linux shell scripting, and vendored the Mermaid.js diagramming library to remove a runtime dependency, accessible company-wide.</li><li>Enforced explicit JSON output contracts and streamlined orchestration routing across LLM scoring modules, cutting processing costs 70% and hardening prompts against injection risks.</li></ul><h4 class="brief__label">Payload</h4><ul class="stack-chips"><li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #3776AB"><svg class="stack-chip__logo" viewBox="-1 -1 14 14" shape-rendering="crispEdges" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="-1" y="-1" width="14" height="14" fill="#f4efe2"></rect><rect x="3" y="0" width="5" height="1" fill="#3776AB"></rect><rect x="3" y="1" width="1" height="1" fill="#3776AB"></rect><rect x="5" y="1" width="4" height="1" fill="#3776AB"></rect><rect x="3" y="2" width="6" height="1